# Helpy Cursor Rules

## Critical Patterns - DO NOT MODIFY

### Bottom Sheets - MUST BE ABOVE BOTTOM NAV

**RULE: Every bottom sheet/modal MUST use `createPortal` to render to `document.body`.**

This ensures bottom sheets ALWAYS appear above the bottom navigation bar, regardless of any CSS stacking contexts.

#### Option 1: Use the BottomSheet Component (Preferred)

```tsx
import BottomSheet from '@/components/ui/BottomSheet';

<BottomSheet isOpen={isOpen} onClose={() => setIsOpen(false)}>
  <BottomSheet.Header>
    <h2 className="text-title text-foreground">Title</h2>
  </BottomSheet.Header>
  <BottomSheet.Body>
    <p>Content</p>
  </BottomSheet.Body>
  <BottomSheet.Footer>
    <button>Action</button>
  </BottomSheet.Footer>
</BottomSheet>
```

#### Option 2: Manual createPortal (for custom modals)

```tsx
import { createPortal } from 'react-dom';

{isOpen && createPortal(
  <div className="fixed inset-0 bg-black/30 backdrop-blur-sm z-[60] flex items-end justify-center bottom-sheet-backdrop">
    {/* Safe area cover */}
    <div className="absolute bottom-0 left-0 right-0 bg-card" style={{ height: 'env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 34px)' }} />
    <div className="bg-card w-full max-w-lg rounded-t-2xl overflow-hidden bottom-sheet-content" style={{ marginBottom: 'env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 34px)' }}>
      {/* Content */}
    </div>
  </div>
, document.body)}
```

#### Why This Matters

- CSS `animation` and `opacity` properties create stacking contexts
- Elements inside a stacking context cannot escape it with z-index
- The Layout component wraps page content, creating potential stacking issues
- `createPortal` renders directly to `document.body`, bypassing all stacking contexts

#### Z-Index Hierarchy

| Element | Z-Index |
|---------|---------|
| Bottom Navigation | `z-10` |
| Sticky Headers | `z-20` |
| Dropdowns | `z-50` |
| **Bottom Sheets/Modals** | `z-[60]` + `createPortal` |
| `.bottom-sheet-backdrop` CSS | `z-index: 9999 !important` |

**NEVER create a bottom sheet without `createPortal` or the `BottomSheet` component!**

---

### Meals Page - LOCKED PATTERN (DO NOT MODIFY)

**The Meals page uses container-based scrolling. DO NOT CHANGE.**

#### Container-Based Scroll (Meals.tsx)
- Outer container: `h-screen bg-background overflow-hidden` (locked to viewport)
- Cards container: `overflow-y-auto scrollbar-hide` with calculated height
- All scrolling happens INSIDE the cards container only
- No page-level scroll, no dual-scroll confusion
- Footer (`helpy-footer`) is INSIDE the cards container

**DO NOT** change the outer container from `h-screen overflow-hidden`.

#### Header Structure (Meals.tsx)
- Standard sticky header matching ToDo (120px, `boxShadow` for bleed-through)
- Week nav has shadow controlled by `isContainerScrolled` state
- **NO overlays** - uses real elements directly

**DO NOT** add overlay patterns or opacity-0 elements.

#### Always-Mounted Pattern (App.tsx)
- Meals is rendered OUTSIDE Layout's keyed container
- Uses `display: block/none` based on activeView
- Passes `isActive={activeView === 'meals'}` prop

**DO NOT** move Meals back into renderView() or add key={} to its wrapper.

#### Layout Fragment Pattern (Layout.tsx)
- When children is null (Meals active), wrapper div is not rendered
- Only bottom nav is rendered, preventing empty 80px div above Meals

**DO NOT** change back to always-render wrapper pattern.

#### Scroll-to-Today Logic (Meals.tsx)
- Uses `getBoundingClientRect()` for accurate container-relative positioning
- Multiple timed attempts [0, 50, 150]ms for reliability
- `hasInitiallyScrolled` ref prevents duplicate scrolls

**DO NOT** change to `offsetTop` or window scroll.

#### Git Pull Warning
If `git pull` conflicts with Meals.tsx, App.tsx, or Layout.tsx:
- **KEEP LOCAL VERSION** with `git checkout --ours <file>`

See `docs/MEALS_SCROLL_FIX.md` for full details.

---

## Code Style

- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Follow existing component patterns
- Keep translations in the `t` object
- Use `useScrollHeader` hook for sticky header animations
- Use `useScrollLock` when modals are open
